  notes: >-
    Conjectural, not peer reviewed. Version 0.11.0 organizes the programme
    around Finite Gradient Closure: finite realized domains and transitions
    with lower and upper closure, while continuation may be unbounded. Nested
    Gradient Spectrum is its H/Q spectral and complexity specialization, using
    QFT modes, EFT coarse-graining, and thermodynamics without claiming a
    dark-sector identity, universal hertz, automatic golden ratio, or
    inevitable observers. NGS-0 executes only the declared finite-band,
    recurrence-eigenvalue, and independent-trial probability controls. DSF-3
    is a documentation-level finite-domain causal-calibration hypothesis, not
    a varying-local-c result. The project uses a
    no-unaccountable-explanatory-variable rule: dark-sector ontology remains
    open, but every replacement must recover the evidence, change a
    predeclared operational prediction, and expose a falsifier; antimatter is
    directly evidenced and treated separately. Stable asymmetry is a
    conditional stability and finite-throughput target, not an axiom. The
    spatial scale-selection controls are not a gravity theory. A corrected
    tetrad audit shows that the minimal ECD axial contact stress is metric
    proportional with zero metric-null contraction, retracting the earlier
    fixed-current NEC claim. FGC-1-SRC1-NL1 closes the same-evaluator
    nonlinear-source premise; CON4 closes conditional boundary-free
    constraints; CTR1/ID1 close regular-centre finite-mass data; DOM4/HYP2
    close a nonzero classical run domain plus sufficient all-spatial-covector
    principal-health gate; BND2 closes the scoped boundary row by causal
    isolation; HLT1 closes the transactional classical-health monitor row on
    synthetic controls; and NUM1 independently validates both numerical
    methods and the affine-measurement route on outcome-blind controls.
    FGC-1-RUN1-SYM1 preserves a PROTO3-era 7/8 structural authorization
    result, while CAL0-PREF2 proves that its last manifest cannot honestly be
    resolved under PROTO3: the declared compact pulse fails the literal
    last-bin spectral rule on every grid and calibration lacks a branch-
    applicability map. No FGC-QR or SGB-L outcome was opened. A premise-only
    FGC-2-SF1-PROTO4 successor is now frozen by PRO4-FRZ1 against immutable
    PROTO3/CAL0 Git blobs, with branch-specific stop ownership and convergence-
    budgeted spectral/constraint admission. FGC-1-HLT2-MON2 now implements
    those successor formulas on static and manufactured controls without
    reading a trajectory. FGC-1-ID2-ALL1 then constructs all seven GR-0 inputs
    and all 35 amplitude/case FGC-QR slices with both methods on three grids;
    its 252 distinct complete-state hashes give 31/35 FGC-QR static passes and
    freeze [5/2, 3] as the only fresh-calibration candidates. These are input-
    contract findings, not mechanism outcomes. The work still exposes an
    unowned SGB-L source/health route and a missing constraint-to-Raychaudhuri
    stability map. Fresh GR-0 calibration, PRO4-HLD1, and holdout execution
    remain false. A nonlinear constraint-
    preserving IBVP, retained-EFT completion, global transition, spectral
    transfer, flux and entropy closure, child topology, and independent
    observational confirmation remain open. The later
    FGC-1-CAL10-PREF15 binder records that the PROTO13 GR-0 continuation
    terminated normally at its first 64-sample temporal-spectrum gate while
    both method-owned spatial/constraint admissions still passed. It derives
    no cause, eligible case, candidate outcome, or physical obstruction; only
    a separately frozen temporal-gate diagnosis may follow. FGC-1-TDG1-FRZ1
    now freezes that diagnosis before reading the terminal histories and proves
    by synthetic counterexample that normalized raw temporal tail fractions
    cancel amplitude convergence, so they are not a general spatial-
    convergence observable for nonzero histories. It preserves the historical
    stop and authorizes only a read-only diagnosis, not a replacement gate or
    trajectory. FGC-1-TDG1-PREF16 now binds that actual-history diagnosis:
    the normalized-ratio defect survives, while 544 of 1728 individual
    records fail, including 395 above the declared amplitude floor, and the
    unnormalized comparison remains incomplete. Only prospective TDG2
    absolute-tail discriminator design may begin. FGC-1-TDG2-FRZ1 now freezes
    that discriminator before reading an actual history: unnormalized
    top-band power, independent Decimal/binary64 arithmetic evidence, a
    conditional interpolation enclosure, and seven no-history controls define
    five descriptive classes. FGC-1-TDG2-PREF17 now binds all 576 actual
    history ladders and 1152 field/derivative classifications. The result is
    mixed: some finest failures contract, a small subset is conditionally
    nonzero, and the unresolved majority is dominated by the conditional
    common-grid interpolation enclosure rather than binary64 DFT arithmetic.
    FGC-1-TDG3-FRZ1 now prospectively freezes two native-grid, no-resampling
    estimators with independent Decimal arithmetic audits and seven synthetic
    controls. FGC-1-TDG3-PREF18 now binds all actual histories. Every one of
    the 92 TDG2 zero-contracting finest classifications survives, none of nine
    tentative nonzero classifications is confirmed, and 104 of 203 enclosure-
    dominated classifications remain unresolved or estimator-dependent.
    Common-grid interpolation is not the sole owner; neither sampled surrogate
    nor their spread is a continuum enclosure. FGC-1-TDG4-FRZ1 now freezes the
    required sampling-identifiability theorem and exact no-history controls:
    the kernel/factorization criterion, smooth between-sample witnesses, an
    independent 64-node alias family, and the sufficient-premise ledger. The
    theorem result was then independently bound by FGC-1-TDG4-PREF19 against
    immutable FRZ1, PROTO4, PROTO13, and CAL10 evidence. Finite samples alone
    do not bound the declared continuum powers on the unrestricted smooth
    class. The old rule is retired only as continuum admission, retained as a
    sampled diagnostic, and CAL10 remains unreclassified. FGC-1-TDG5-FRZ1 now
    freezes one permitted replacement architecture: a complete-state cubic-
    Hermite endpoint value/slope map plus same-grid one-step/two-half-step
    refinement. Exact finite-dimensional and method-order controls pass.
    FGC-1-TDG5-PREF20 independently rederives the map, both half restrictions,
    the continuous cubic-extremum candidate theorem, the conditional
    Richardson factors, and the immutable engine's fresh endpoint-RHS shape.
    FGC-1-TDG5-IMP1 then implements and synthetically validates both atomic
    method-owned coarse/fine pairs and the continuous outward binary64
    candidate/Bernstein envelope. FGC-1-TDG6-FRZ1 then freezes the three-level
    one-full/two-half/four-quarter admission, exact outward three-halves order
    test, complete 18-channel finest-pair debit, and bounded temporal retry
    semantics without an absolute or outcome-scaled tolerance.
    FGC-1-TDG6-PREF21 independently derives the quarter maps, interval theorem,
    channel/debit reduction, and source-shape feasibility and authorizes only
    compositor implementation and synthetic qualification.
    FGC-1-TDG6-IMP2 now implements and synthetically qualifies that production-
    shaped compositor for both methods, including independent tracer shadows,
    fine-only atomic state/tracer/debit commit, durable temporal retries,
    checkpoint restoration, failure ownership, and mutation controls.
    FGC-1-PRO14-FRZ1 now binds the exact prospective successor to immutable
    commit 27badf9 and all six fixed t=23/16 restart payloads. The old
    64-sample quantity is nonveto-only; TDG6 instead governs every accepted
    post-restart macro step. Its debit begins at restart and proves no earlier
    temporal, global PDE, or Raychaudhuri error bound. FGC-1-HLT12-MON12 now
    binds that successor to the exact restart payloads, pinned runtime, CAL11
    plan, temporal-aware member, checkpoint contract, and dedicated runner.
    Its bounded fine-only-commit, retry-ownership, rollback, checkpoint-first
    idempotent terminal publication,
    namespace, and nonpromotion controls pass, authorizing exactly one
    recoverable fresh GR-0 continuation without advancing a production event.
    Calibration completion, eligible GR-0, candidate branches, and physical
    results remain closed. FGC-1-CAL11-PREF22 then binds the PROTO14 terminal
    invalid-runtime result: event 23 remains complete, event 24 aborts at the
    pre-shadow validator, and every member is restored to zero post-restart
    accepted macro steps, temporal retries, and TDG6 debit. This is an
    instrument outcome, not a constraint, spatial, temporal-admission, or
    scientific GR-0 obstruction. FGC-1-TDG7-FRZ1 now freezes the prospective
    stage-safe exact-binary64 shared-lattice diagnosis: `G=8Q` makes the actual
    RK4/SSPRK3 `c={0,1/2,1}` stage times and endpoints exact, while the old
    independently rounded historical boundaries remain distinct from the new
    `8Q` selection. It derives the arithmetic root cause while leaving the
    runtime unrepaired. FGC-1-TDG7-PREF23 now independently binds that theorem,
    including the historical source-stage contract, and authorizes only a later
    runtime-repair implementation plus synthetic qualification. FGC-1-TDG7-IMP3
    now implements and synthetically qualifies that repair on deterministic
    controls, without reading campaign history or creating a namespace. It
    exposes the stateless discarded-retry limitation; only prospective
    replacement-protocol freeze design with a durable cursor is authorized.
    PROTO15/HLT13 then establish only a synthetic durable-cursor instrument.
    PROTO16 freezes the missing successful common-event lifecycle and the
    externally anchored GenesisSpec contract. FGC-1-PRO16-PREF24 then makes a
    static completeness diagnosis: the receipt cycle is removed but the
    remaining successor cursor/high-water and external generation-zero
    construction rules are not frozen to the deterministic standard. PROTO17
    subsequently freezes the pure construction of the six-member generation
    zero and common-event successor mappings, but implements no side-effectful
    runtime. FGC-1-PRO17-PREF25 independently reconstructs that abstract
    construction without importing the PROTO17 implementation and reproduces
    its three synthetic hashes. FGC-1-HLT14-MON14 now completes the authorized
    synthetic-only production-shaped authority, raw-bundle, runtime, and
    common-event qualification in `72=4+6+18+44` unique cases. It separately
    reproduces those sealed hashes and fully rehashes temporary real-NPZ
    inputs, but raw hashes are input-dependent and exception faults are not
    power-loss proof. Actual raw-byte validation, launch authority,
    historical-payload replay, and namespace/foreign-store rejection remain
    required and uncompleted production duties. Only a separate
    production-prelaunch successor design is authorized; no namespace,
    pretrajectory operation, calibration, eligibility, candidate, or physical
    result is authorized.
    EFT1 stays at 3/12, and neither candidate evolution nor a physical
    transition is authorized.
    FGC-1-PRO18-FRZ1 then freezes only the real two-source-container/fresh-
    output production-prelaunch chain: FGC-1-PRO18-PREF26, immutable
    FGC-1-PRO18-AUTH1, FGC-1-HLT15-GEN1, and FGC-1-PRO18-PREF27. It opens no
    raw archive or history and creates no namespace. At that freeze boundary,
    all four HLT14 production duties were required and uncompleted; only PREF26
    implementation/design was authorized, with no pretrajectory, calibration,
    candidate, EFT, transition, or physical result.
    FGC-1-PRO18-PREF26 now completes the bounded read-only binding of the two
    actual PROTO12/RSP2 checkpoint containers, their byte-identical external
    and embedded legacy journals, and all six selected restart identities. It
    discharges only actual raw-byte/hash recomputation and semantic historical-
    payload replay. External Git/blob/live-import authority remains for AUTH1,
    while namespace reuse and foreign-store rejection remain for PREF27.
    PREF26 is not launch authority, constructs no final GenesisSpec, accesses
    no future output root, advances no trajectory, and authorizes no
    calibration, candidate, EFT, transition, or physical claim.
    FGC-1-PRO18-AUTH1 now constructs the canonical commit-independent,
    calibration-only authority payload. It binds the compact PREF26 evidence,
    exact complete GR-0/amplitude-3 GenesisSpec, production source closure
    including the standard-library-only HLT15 bootstrap/authority module,
    exact evolution environment, raw-source config, and deterministic fresh
    campaign ID. At that historical boundary it was deliberately not
    self-authenticating and advanced no state. FGC-1-HLT15-GEN1 has now used
    immutable AUTH1 commit 2e3373a... to validate the external Git/blob/live-
    byte tuple, numerical environment, imports, and actual six-state reimport
    in one detached invocation before the first output-root observation and
    atomic generation-zero installation. The resulting checkpoint contains
    six FRESH_READY members and zero accepted macro-steps, retries, or debits.
    FGC-1-PRO18-PREF27 independently authenticates
    that exact eight-leaf store and records byte-identical reuse,
    self-consistent foreign-store, and arriving-root no-clobber behavior on
    disposable same-filesystem roots. All four declared HLT14 production
    duties are complete, but no state
    advance, calibration, GR-0 eligibility, candidate, EFT, transition, or
    physical result is authorized.
    PRO19 subsequently preserved five finite accepted RK4-2049 macro-steps,
    recovered and independently bound a metadata-only generation-eight retry
    cursor, and authenticated one committed SID3 resume image. A guarded live
    preflight passed, but the bounded resume appended only generation nine's
    generic HLT16AttemptError invalid-terminal record and terminal lock.
    FGC-1-PRO19-PREF28 proves that all accepted member maps are unchanged and
    no new state or payload exists. The persisted record exposes no exception
    message or root-cause diagnosis. Event 23, GR-0 calibration, SGB-L,
    FGC-QR, DEF1, retained-EFT, transition, and every physical claim remain
    incomplete.
